B T49 B468 | caption=\n\n\n<figure>\n  <figcaption><strong>Figure 1</strong> A simplified pathway showing excitatory circulatory signaling from SFO and OVLT, which are circumventricular organs lacking blood brain barrier, passing to the adjacent PVN in the hypothalamus and RVLM in the brainstem, causing an efferent sympathetic nerve response from the intermediolateral column of the spinal cord to the heart and blood vessels, resulting in increased heart rate and increased blood pressure associated with vasoconstriction.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n\nBy various studies it has been identified that elevated SNA is observed in obesity, especially in the kidney and hindlimb, for which a leptin increase and hypothalamic melanocortin activity elevation are predominant activities [127]. | unit=S162
